# Sliding `rate`: cold, one sample, two samples, and a window emptied
# underneath them. `Rate.r` is a payload slot, so `verify recordings` compares
# the value. A pump reads the samples earlier pumps absorbed ([LSER.8.6]):
#
#   pump 1  t = 0: cold, -1.0
#   pump 2  t = 2 s: [10 @0], one sample, no elapsed time: null, -1.0
#   pump 3  t = 3 s: [10 @0, 30 @2s]: (30 - 10) * 1e9 / 2e9 = 10.0
#   pump 4  t = 23 s, window (13 s, 23 s]: every sample has left it, cold, -1.0
#
# Every assert changes its value, since a no-op reassert would not fire the
# rule ([LFAC.2.5.1]).
# @spec [LSER.16.9] [LSER.19.8]
assert Flow k=a v=10.0
pump
advance 2000000000
assert Flow k=a v=30.0
pump
advance 1000000000
assert Flow k=a v=31.0
pump
advance 20000000000
assert Flow k=a v=32.0
pump
